KP.talentNotes={"WARRIOR:Improved Rend":"Rend's bleed does 35% more. With Bloodthrill your main-hand hits on a Rended target can light up Overpower, so Rend is kept up anyway; this makes that upkeep pay for itself.","WARRIOR:Improved Tactical Mastery":"Keeps more of your rage when you change stance. Arms swaps to Battle Stance for Overpower and Berserker for Whirlwind; a tank swaps between Defensive and the others. Without it a swap throws most of your rage away.","WARRIOR:Improved Overpower":"+50% crit chance on Overpower: almost every Overpower crits, and each crit also feeds Deep Wounds and Impale.","WARRIOR:Bloodthrill":"Main-hand hits on a target with your Rend have a 20% chance to allow Overpower. Overpower is one of your cheapest, hardest-hitting attacks, and bosses rarely dodge, so this is how Arms gets to use it often.","WARRIOR:Improved Slam":"Slam stops delaying your swing and gets a shorter cooldown and cast. Without it Slam costs you white damage; with it Slam is a free extra attack between Mortal Strikes.","WARRIOR:Booming Voice":"Shouts cost 25% less rage and reach 50% farther. Battle Shout is refreshed all fight, so the rage saved goes into attacks, and the whole group stays in range.","WARRIOR:Reckless Swings":"Your next 4 swings give 5 extra rage each (20 in all) for 8 sec. Rage is what limits a warrior, so that's more Mortal Strikes, Bloodthirsts and Heroic Strikes.","WARRIOR:Improved Whirlwind":"Whirlwind comes back 2 sec sooner and hits the closest enemy 30% harder, so it's a strong single-target attack too, not only for packs.","WARRIOR:Lingering Rage":"Rage starts to fade 2 sec later per point after a fight: you walk into the next leveling pull with some of the last one's rage.","WARRIOR:Death Wish":"+20% physical damage for 30 sec (and immune to Fear). A big burst for the Execute phase or a hard pull.","WARRIOR:Improved Berserker Rage":"Berserker Rage gives 10 rage instantly and frees you from slows: extra rage and mobility on a short cooldown.","WARRIOR:Improved Heroic Strike":"Heroic Strike costs 3 less rage. It's what every warrior presses with spare rage, so the saving adds up over a fight; it's also a cheap first row point.","WARRIOR:Improved Charge":"Charge gives 6 more rage: you start every pull with an attack ready.","WARRIOR:Improved Bloodrage":"Bloodrage gives 50% more rage: a rage boost at the pull, which is when a tank needs threat most.","WARRIOR:Improved Revenge":"Revenge does 60% more damage. It's cheap and comes up often while tanking (after a dodge, parry or block), so it's a strong threat button.","WARRIOR:Last Stand":"An emergency button: +30% of your health for 20 sec. Saves the raid when healers fall behind.","WARRIOR:Master of Defense":"Every dodge or parry with a shield gives 5 rage. Tanks get rage from being hit; this adds rage even from hits that miss you, so you have more for threat.","WARRIOR:Defiance":"+15% threat in Defensive Stance with a shield. Threat is the tank's real job, and the damage math doesn't count threat modifiers, so its value doesn't show in the numbers.","WARRIOR:Improved Sunder Armor":"Sunder Armor costs 3 less rage. Tanks press it a lot early in a fight (5 stacks for the raid, plus threat), so the rage saved goes into Shield Slam and Revenge.","WARRIOR:Improved Shield Wall":"Shield Wall's cooldown drops by 11 minutes, so you can use it on every hard boss instead of once a night.","WARRIOR:Deflection":"More parry: fewer hits land, and parries feed Master of Defense rage and Revenge.","WARRIOR:Anticipation":"+Defense: fewer hits, crits and crushing blows land on you.","WARRIOR:Shield Specialization":"More block chance with a shield, and blocks give rage: both survival and threat.","WARRIOR:Focused Rage":"Your attacks cost 3 less rage, so you can press more Shield Slams, Revenges and Sunders.","WARRIOR:Concussion Blow":"A 5-second stun: for emergencies, dangerous adds and interrupting casters that can't be kicked. No damage, so the numbers can't see it.","WARRIOR:Sweeping Strikes":"Your next hits also strike a second enemy. Strong on two-target fights and while leveling, and it's needed to reach Mortal Strike.","HUNTER:Improved Arcane Shot":"Arcane Shot's cooldown drops by 1.5 sec, so you fit more of them between Auto Shots.","HUNTER:Improved Tracking":"+5% damage to whatever type you're tracking (Beasts, Humanoids, Undead...). Pick the boss's type and it's a flat damage boost; the planner doesn't know the target's type, so it can't count it.","HUNTER:Survivalist":"+10% health: fewer deaths to area damage and pulls that go wrong.","HUNTER:Surefooted":"More hit (fewer misses) and shorter slows on you. Hit is worth the most until you reach the cap; see Hit on the panel.","HUNTER:Deadly Aspects":"With Aspect of the Hawk, Auto Shot has a 10% chance to give +30% attack speed for 12 sec (melee: same with Aspect of the Beast). The planner doesn't simulate this proc yet, so its value doesn't show.","HUNTER:Endurance Training":"Your pet has 15% more health and armor, so it survives longer while tanking mobs for you.","HUNTER:Focused Fire":"+2% damage for you and your pet while the pet is out.","HUNTER:Unleashed Fury":"Pets and hawks deal 15% more damage. Pet damage is server-side (not in the game files), so the planner can't count it.","HUNTER:Ferocity":"+10% crit for pets and hawks. Pet damage isn't in the files, so the planner can't count it.","HUNTER:Summon Hawk":"Hawks dive-bomb your target for 18 sec (two at once). Their damage isn't in the game files, so it's left out of the numbers.","HUNTER:Spirit Bond":"You and your pet regenerate 1% health every 5 sec: less downtime while leveling.","HUNTER:Frenzy":"Your pet gets +30% attack speed for 8 sec after a crit. A big pet damage boost the planner can't count (pet damage is server-side).","HUNTER:Clever Traps":"Immolation and Explosive Trap deal 30% more and Freezing/Frost Trap last 30% longer. In Forever traps work in combat, so a melee Survival Hunter keeps using them.","HUNTER:Deterrence":"+25% dodge and parry for 10 sec: the emergency button when something turns on you.","HUNTER:Counterattack":"After you parry, a strike that also roots the target for 5 sec. Free damage and control in melee.","HUNTER:Efficiency":"Shots, stings and melee abilities cost 15% less mana. Hunters run out of mana in long fights; this keeps the shots going."};
